# Urban Retreat: "{2}, Return a tapped creature you control to its owner's hand: Put this card from your hand onto the
# battlefield." The creature is chosen as the cost is paid, once the mana abilities are activated (CR 602.2b, 601.2g-h):
# Bot1's only creature, Birds of Paradise, is untapped when Bot1 activates the ability from the hand, so it is offered
# because the Birds could tap for mana while it is paid. Bot1 pays {2} with the Forest and the Birds, and only then
# chooses the creature to return: the Birds, tapped for that very mana. Urban Retreat enters tapped, the Birds in hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Birds of Paradise
Urban Retreat
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Birds of Paradise.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Birds of Paradise.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand.Urban Retreat.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Birds of Paradise.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Birds of Paradise)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
